{
  "assembly_notes": "One carcass part carries the case shell, the support base, the zone split (mid rail or centre divider), the hinge mullions and the runner rails. Door leaves and drawers are separate moving parts and both mechanisms are always present. The host publishes a plan profile and a clear opening, so leaves and drawer fronts are struck from the host front curve, and leaf size, hinge line, track run, tray width, box depth and travel all derive from the zone split and from N. No combination is excluded and no overlap allowance is emitted.",
